// A tied chord on a TAB staff: each string's tie must hug its OWN fret digit.
// LilyPond sets every TabNoteHead's staff-position to the string line its
// exclusive fret allocation chose (tab-note-heads-engraver.cc), and the ties
// follow the heads. Resolving each note's string per-note (auto-fret) instead
// piled every tie onto one low string; here they spread across strings 1-3.
octave absolute
part gt { clef treble_8 tuning guitar }
section A {
  gt { <c' e' g'>2~ <c' e' g'>4 r4 }
}
form main { A }
score main "tab-chord-tie" {
  staff gt
  tab gt as full
}

// ⚠ THE TAB ASKS FOR `as full` EXPLICITLY (2026-08-29). A tab beside a notation staff
// of the same part now defaults to `as numbers`, which draws no stems, beams, dots,
// tuplet numbers or ties -- and this book is ABOUT one of those, so without the clause
// it would keep passing while testing nothing it claims to.
